Native Mojo experiment derived from the MIT Perbase, goose-perbase and
c-perbase application algorithms by Seth Stadick. The Goose application
reference is e84cc768234f3332237c609fe934178eaf46ebb6. C Perbase's optimized local
source was also consulted; it is not linked into this application.

The BAM reader in mojo-bio retains the Seth Stadick and Pascal Hertleif
MIT attribution for Goose Seqair/Seqair-derived algorithms. libdeflate 1.26 is
vendored in mojo-libdeflate with its original COPYING file. No Goose-generated
C or Rust code is linked. native/perbase.c is application-specific POSIX output
glue; reusable pthread/CPU-count glue lives in mojo-threads.

Integer formatting uses ExtraMojo, which retains its own license and attribution
notices.

CoffeeVampir3/Mojo-Linuxperiments revision
0637c1082ffd43e9fb561f24163d1a4a5e0e09f0 was evaluated, not copied or linked.
It uses obsolete Mojo APIs and raw clone/TLS setup not validated for this
allocation-heavy application. Persistent pthreads are used instead.

tests/compare.py imports an external Goose test suite read-only, preserving
its assertions. Python/pysam and reference binaries are validation tools,
not application runtime dependencies.
